  "notMeasuredHere": [
    "The wipe-pin-v1 binary LTO.md says runs A-D were made with, sha256 aa7329c3d9ba002915f885624c17d6da1418aa39a2b762d1655e83786e6f0a66. Its OUTCOME columns are covered: the v2 re-runs above reproduce run A's -O2 row, run B's -O1 row and run C's levels (over all 113 files rather than C's sample of 10). What is not covered, and cannot be: run A's (ii) columns predate the link-time stderr line the probe now requires and grades, so a v1 run today is unreproducible by design rather than merely unrun.",
    "Run D's --force-fallback path (post-LTO code read through precodegen + llc instead of --lto-emit-asm). The preflight passed in every run above, so the fallback was never taken and its -O2 figures were not re-measured.",
    "The --sample, --plan and --files selections of either probe.",
    "Anything about a second machine. These eight invocations and all of LTO.md's originals share one WSL host, so agreement between them is not independent replication."
