  "provenance": {
    "numbers": "parsed out of the captured stdout of the eight invocations by a THROWAWAY script, then compared cell by cell against LTO.md before being written here: 188 cells, 0 disagreements. That script is not tracked and neither is the lab output it read, so this record is no more re-derivable from the tree than a hand transcription would be -- which is exactly why test/lto-regate.test.mjs compares it against LTO.md rather than trusting it. The probes refuse --write-data (exit 4), so no tool wrote this file as part of a run.",
    "gate": "read from the first line of each invocation's captured output, where the probes write the gate summary to stderr. Nothing in the lab persists it, so the gate fields here are not recoverable from the lab afterwards -- they rest on those captures. The configurations and discriminating values were separately confirmed by calling runSpikeGate directly and printing verdict rather than by reading the summary line.",
    "wallClockSeconds": "from `time` on each invocation, several of them sharing the machine with another, and expected to differ elsewhere. A per-level invocation covering three levels reports one figure for all three."
